  "slug": "high-nanoantenna-b3b2",
  "summary": "Five preprints from 13–18 November 2026 report quantified resonance control via coupling, material choice and environment in metasurfaces, resonators and nanoantennas.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is control of resonant optical response through coupling, composition or environment. In silicon BIC metasurfaces, strong QBIC-GMR coupling yields intrinsic circular dichroism of 0.995 with Q = 1083 at 1653.9 nm. MAPbBr3 BIC resonances are tuned reversibly and continuously by HCl/HBr vapor anion exchange. Coupled TiO2 and perovskite-coated microresonators show tunable whispering gallery mode hybridization, with non-monotonic behavior reported. In plasmonics, hollow-core fiber-coupled nanoantenna arrays deliver polarization-resilient THz generation and detection (2.1 mW, 145 dB), while a coaxial nanoantenna study maps inverse Faraday magnetization across Au, Ag, Cu, Al and TiN. The new element is the quantified tuning of resonances across platforms, spanning chiral response, chemical reconfiguration and THz instrumentation. Most results are numerical or theoretical, except where experimental metrics are stated.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
